<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sangram Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sangram Shah was a Gond king of Garha-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/katanga">Katanga</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the early 16th century. He expanded the kingdom from its base near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jabalpur">Jabalpur</a> to dozens of forts across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narmada-river">Narmada</a> valley, making it one of the largest states of the region. His daughter-in-law Rani Durgavati later ruled the kingdom and died resisting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> in 1564.</p></div>
